<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Ecia started as buy.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Ecia started as buy.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>JP Morgan Securities analyst Camilla Darwin started coverage of French auto parts maker Ecia Thursday with a rating of buy.</p>
<p>-- Over the next few years, we expect Ecia to continue to broaden its businesses,&quot; she wrote in a report.</p>
<p>-- &quot;... We believe the group's strong cash generation, which should give it the flexibility to invest in growth, supports a share price of FF 1,150 by the end of 1998.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Ecia is 68-percent owned by PSA Peugeot Citroen .</p>
<p>((--Ian Simpson, Wall Street desk, (212) 859-1879))</p>
</text>
